<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
   Backup/transfer rules for API 31+ (see backup_rules.xml for API 26-30).
   See https://developer.android.com/about/versions/12/backup-restore#xml-changes

   Empty rules mean "back everything up", so these exclusions are load-bearing (Issue #62):

   - budget_database (+ its -wal/-shm sidecars) is the Room DB — budget amounts, note
     contents, reminder text. It has no field-level encryption at rest, and an OS-level
     backup would bypass any in-app lock (the roadmap's biometric lock for Budget/Notes
     would be defeated by it). Firebase sync, not Android backup, is this app's story for
     getting data onto a new device.
   - device_identity holds the per-install UUID that keys this device's screen-time docs
     at users/{uid}/devices/{deviceId}. Restoring it onto a second device would make both
     devices write to the same doc and clobber each other's screen time.
   - note_attachments holds the images the user attached to notes (Issue #191). The rationale
     for excluding the DB applies verbatim: a photographed receipt or document is at least as
     sensitive as the note text it belongs to, and backing the image up while withholding the
     caption is the worst of both — the payload leaves the device while the user's mental model
     says notes aren't backed up. It also cannot restore usefully on its own: without the notes
     table these are orphaned bytes no row points at.
   - daily_apex_tip is a local cache of AI-generated text based on personal tracker totals.
     It is deliberately device-local and a dated response would be stale after restore.
   - budget_settings holds the overall monthly spending ceiling — a financial figure, and the
     one DataStore value that is data about the user rather than a device preference.
   - papers_discovery carries reading-interest bookkeeping.
   - account_identity records which Firebase account the local Room data belongs to (Issue #186).
     Restoring it onto a device whose Room data came from elsewhere would make the account-switch
     guard believe the data is already the right user's and skip the wipe.
   - database_key holds the SQLCipher passphrase (Issue #117), wrapped by *this device's*
     Android Keystore key. Restoring it without budget_database would be harmless on its own,
     but budget_database IS excluded above — so without this exclusion too, a restore leaves a
     wrapped passphrase on the new device that its Keystore can never decrypt (Issue #206).
     loadOrCreatePassphrase() then fails, and the app falls back to a brand-new *unencrypted*
     database forever, silently defeating Issue #117's guarantee. Excluding it means a restored
     device mints its own fresh passphrase and its own fresh encrypted database, same as a new
     install — exactly like device_identity and account_identity above.

   Deliberately still backed up: reminder/note/study/currency/security settings. Those are device
   preferences, not personal data, and carrying them to a new device is the point of a backup.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="database" path="budget_database" />
        <exclude domain="database" path="budget_database-wal" />
        <exclude domain="database" path="budget_database-shm" />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="device_identity.xml" />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="database_key.xml" />
        <exclude domain="file" path="note_attachments" />
        <exclude domain="file" path="datastore/daily_apex_tip.preferences_pb" />
        <exclude domain="file" path="datastore/budget_settings.preferences_pb" />
        <exclude domain="file" path="datastore/papers_discovery.preferences_pb" />
        <exclude domain="file" path="datastore/account_identity.preferences_pb" />
    </cloud-backup>
    <!-- Declared explicitly: an absent <device-transfer> silently falls back to the
         <cloud-backup> rules above, which is right today, but that coupling is not
         obvious to the next reader. -->
    <device-transfer>
        <exclude domain="database" path="budget_database" />
        <exclude domain="database" path="budget_database-wal" />
        <exclude domain="database" path="budget_database-shm" />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="device_identity.xml" />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="database_key.xml" />
        <exclude domain="file" path="note_attachments" />
        <exclude domain="file" path="datastore/daily_apex_tip.preferences_pb" />
        <exclude domain="file" path="datastore/budget_settings.preferences_pb" />
        <exclude domain="file" path="datastore/papers_discovery.preferences_pb" />
        <exclude domain="file" path="datastore/account_identity.preferences_pb" />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
